# Operations Registry

Owner rules live in the Service concept, not in this rule.

- [operations-registry](../../docs/knowledge/services/operations-registry.md)
- [granot-lifecycle source-policy](../../docs/knowledge/granot-lifecycle/source-policy.md)
- [catalog](../../docs/knowledge/services/catalog.md)

Software-only notes that are not in those files may stay below (env, ngrok, collection suffix, script names).

- Routes and runtime consumers import `src/services/operationsRegistry/` commands, queries, and resolvers rather than registry models. Runtime Granot policy reads go through `src/services/granotLifecycle/sourcePolicy.ts`.
- Owner Granot create is `POST /api/v1/admin/granot-crm-sources` via `ownerGranotNames.ts`. Atomic setup is `POST /api/v1/admin/operations-registry/lead-source-setups` and `/preview` via `leadSourceSetup.ts`. Aggregate Owner reads are `GET /api/v1/admin/operations-registry/lead-sources` and `/:id` via `leadSourceProjection.ts` + `findingTranslation.ts`. Label mappings live on `GET/POST /api/v1/admin/source-label-mappings`.
- Registry mutations require a verified signed Owner actor. Canonical signing includes admin ID, normalized email, role, timestamp, request ID, HTTP method, and path using `VANTAGE_ADMIN_PROXY_SIGNING_SECRET`. Optional replay-window and preview compatibility settings live in `src/services/operationsRegistry/config.ts`. Never document secret values.
- Domain mutation and `operations_registry_changes` insert share one Mongo transaction. Audit failure aborts the mutation. Cache invalidation occurs only after commit. Audit snapshots must be bounded and redact secrets, credentials, tokens, authorization values, and provider payloads.
- Migration scripts under `scripts/migrations/` are dry-run by default, reject historical/unknown databases, require explicit [REDACTED] apply confirmation, write deterministic redacted manifests, and never import historical models.
- Granot source classification is `scripts/migrations/granot-lifecycle-source-registry.ts` plus the checked-in manifest. `--scope=best_relocation_creation_policy` and `--scope=link_only_automation_sources` are the only scoped apply modes.
- CRM Source texting is `GranotCrmSource.outbound_sms`. Owner enable/disable is `setGranotCrmSourceOutboundSms` (no `daily_cap` on the Owner command; stored field is copied through). Leaving `create_if_missing` also turns `outbound_sms.enabled` off in the same `createOrUpdateGranotCrmSource` mutation. `create_if_missing` does not send texts. Default backfill is `pnpm migration:granot-crm-source-outbound-sms`. Best Relocation enable is `pnpm migration:granot-crm-source-sms-best-relocation`. Production posture stays in [`lifecycle-activation-flags-and-source-policies.md`](../../docs/granot-lead-lifecycle/lifecycle-activation-flags-and-source-policies.md); do not copy that table here.
